WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.330
Day 0.

2
00:00:01.380 --> 00:00:06.620
An egg is fertilised, and a new
genetic code exists for the first time.

3
00:00:06.670 --> 00:00:11.650
Around day 14, a faint line
appears: the primitive streak.

4
00:00:11.700 --> 00:00:15.650
Until then, one embryo can
still split into twins.

5
00:00:15.700 --> 00:00:19.250
So before day 14, is there one individual,

6
00:00:19.300 --> 00:00:21.850
two, or not yet anyone?

7
00:00:21.900 --> 00:00:25.600
When does a developing human
start to count as someone?

8
00:00:25.650 --> 00:00:28.560
And would knowing that
settle the abortion debate?

9
00:00:28.610 --> 00:00:32.230
In this mission, you'll place
the main answers on one timeline,

10
00:00:32.280 --> 00:00:34.320
from conception to birth.

11
00:00:34.370 --> 00:00:37.130
Then you'll hear religious
and secular voices,

12
00:00:37.180 --> 00:00:39.640
and find they don't split neatly.

13
00:00:39.690 --> 00:00:44.450
Your mission: find out when a developing
human starts to count as someone,

14
00:00:44.500 --> 00:00:46.210
and whether that would settle it.
